PRIVATE SECTOR & PUBLIC SECTOR
India is a Mixed Economy, where both private and public (government) enterprises are allowed to
operate. Therefore, Indian economy may be classified into two sectors:
Private Sector,
It includes all those enterprises
which are managed and owned
by individuals or group of
individuals.
Public Sector
It includes all those enterprises
which are managed and owned
partly or wholly by the Central or
State Government. The
government participates in the
economic activities of the country
through these enterprises.
