PRIVATE SECTOR & PUBLIC SECTOR
The Industrial Policy Resolutions of 1948 and 1956 emphasised a
dominant role for the public sector.
A few industries were exclusively reserved for the public sector. Entry of
private sector was restricted through licensing.
However, dominance of Public Sector tor about 4 decades hampered
the process of growth and development.
As a result, In the '1991 Industrial Policy, government opted for
disinvestment of public sector, enhancing role of private sector and
encouraging foreign direct investment.
So, after the reforms of 1991, Indian Economy consists of public sector
units, private sector enterprises and global enterprises.
