DEPARTMENTAL UNDERTAKING
Features of Departmental Undertaking
Finance: It is financed by the government through
allocation of funds in the Annual General Budget of
Parliament. Government Treasury provides finances and
revenue earned is also paid into the treasury.
Accounting System: This organisation is also subject to
accounting and audit controls as applicable to other
Government activities.
Management: It is managed and controlled by a
government department and is subject to direct control of
the ministry.
