DEPARTMENTAL UNDERTAKING
Limitations of Departmental Undertaking
Red Tapism: Even for routine matters and day-to-day operations, prior
sanction of the relevant authority is necessary. The enterprise is bound by
bureaucratic procedures and rules. This creates unavoidable problems in
functioning of the organisation.
Undue Government Interference: There is a lot of political interference
through the ministry.
Indifferent to Consumers' Needs: These enterprises are somewhat insensitive
to consumer needs and do not provide adequate services to them.
